WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:07.339 --> 00:00:12.350
"Then as I turned back to my work, I noticed
something in the corner of my eye.

00:00:12.350 --> 00:00:14.360
Something was standing in my room now."

00:00:14.360 --> 00:00:22.680
Hello, and welcome to Al Dente Creepypasta,
horror stories cooked to perfection with a

00:00:22.680 --> 00:00:25.650
splash of red sauce.

00:00:25.650 --> 00:00:30.040
My name is CZ and I will be your server this
episode.

00:00:30.040 --> 00:00:35.840
Today's stories are perfect for a cozy night
of studying, relaxing and getting the chills

00:00:35.840 --> 00:00:41.570
running down your spine at the absolute horror
that's about to unfold.

00:00:41.570 --> 00:00:49.809
Make sure you get comfortable, and let's dig
right in.

00:00:49.809 --> 00:00:50.809
---

00:00:50.809 --> 00:00:54.450
Listening to music has always been my favorite
part of winding down when I get home every

00:00:54.450 --> 00:00:55.450
evening.

00:00:55.450 --> 00:01:01.110
Lately, I have really taken a liking to relaxing
in my room and jamming to some lo-fi chill

00:01:01.110 --> 00:01:02.450
music.

00:01:02.450 --> 00:01:06.820
Every night before I go to bed, I'll toss
on a YouTube stream, kick back and talk to

00:01:06.820 --> 00:01:10.240
strangers in the chat for a bit before logging
out for the night.

00:01:10.240 --> 00:01:15.060
I always find it interesting how this seems
to be the only internet chat section in the

00:01:15.060 --> 00:01:19.960
known universe where people always get along,
and I feel like the chill music vibe has to

00:01:19.960 --> 00:01:22.029
have something to do with it.

00:01:22.029 --> 00:01:25.939
Lately I've started to notice that the same
group of people who tend to go online every

00:01:25.939 --> 00:01:27.509
day around the same time.

00:01:27.509 --> 00:01:30.619
Would it be too weird to call them my friends?

00:01:30.619 --> 00:01:32.399
Even though we haven't met?

00:01:32.399 --> 00:01:37.240
We all have similar interests, and it feels
like we can talk about anything: Cowboy Bebop,

00:01:37.240 --> 00:01:42.659
old school video games, our favorite YouTubers
and even or burning hatred for our respective

00:01:42.659 --> 00:01:43.659
English teachers.

00:01:43.659 --> 00:01:47.380
I was chatting on the stream at our usual
time when a channel popped into the conversation

00:01:47.380 --> 00:01:51.340
and wrote the words: ROLL CALL in all caps.

00:01:51.340 --> 00:01:57.240
Random people started writing their location
in the chat: Chicago, Los Angeles, Tokyo.

00:01:57.240 --> 00:02:01.060
Figuring there was no harm in simply putting
a city, I typed my mine into the chat and

00:02:01.060 --> 00:02:03.689
continued to read where some of the others
were from.

00:02:03.689 --> 00:02:08.709
That's when I started noticing that quite
a few of my 'friends' were close by.

00:02:08.709 --> 00:02:10.020
Really close by.

00:02:10.020 --> 00:02:14.270
I kind of daydreamed about what it would be
like if we met in real life, and as if to

00:02:14.270 --> 00:02:19.519
read my mind, one of the regulars in the chat,
"ShadowHand1133" pointed out that we were

00:02:19.519 --> 00:02:22.129
all actually really close to each other.

00:02:22.129 --> 00:02:26.689
One thing led to another, and I know this
was a stupid idea, but we decided to meet

00:02:26.689 --> 00:02:27.689
up.

00:02:27.689 --> 00:02:31.409
I justified it in my head by telling myself
that we had all spoken to each other almost

00:02:31.409 --> 00:02:33.069
every night on the chat.

00:02:33.069 --> 00:02:36.379
It's not like anyone appeared out of the blue
and asked us to meet.

00:02:36.379 --> 00:02:37.849
It felt safe.

00:02:37.849 --> 00:02:39.739
And they felt like friends.

00:02:39.739 --> 00:02:44.310
I’ll just say this right now, because I’m
sure you think you know where this is going.

00:02:44.310 --> 00:02:48.569
Trusting the people I was talking to online
was not necessarily where I went wrong in

00:02:48.569 --> 00:02:49.780
this story.

00:02:49.780 --> 00:02:55.260
Actually, it may have been my saving grace
-- but there was one other thing I overlooked

00:02:55.260 --> 00:03:01.890
-- that led to what I can only describe as
the scariest encounter of my life.

00:03:01.890 --> 00:03:06.870
After school, I rode my bike to the 7/11 we
all decided to meet at around the edge of

00:03:06.870 --> 00:03:07.870
town.

00:03:07.870 --> 00:03:11.530
I got there a few minutes early and sat on
the curb to wait for the others.

00:03:11.530 --> 00:03:13.579
I had no faces to look out for.

00:03:13.579 --> 00:03:18.909
We only actually knew each other by username,
so everyone I saw walking in and out of the

00:03:18.909 --> 00:03:24.469
convenience store was potentially one of us,
and I was imagining each new face I saw linking

00:03:24.469 --> 00:03:25.540
up with a name.

00:03:25.540 --> 00:03:30.480
But over the course of the next 20 minutes
nobody approached me, and I didn’t see any

00:03:30.480 --> 00:03:35.209
messages from the others, even though I tried
hitting them up to see where they were at.

00:03:35.209 --> 00:03:39.159
I was beginning to think that I was the only
one who showed when I heard a voice behind

00:03:39.159 --> 00:03:40.159
me.

00:03:40.159 --> 00:03:41.159
“Hey.”

00:03:41.159 --> 00:03:47.049
I turned to see a man -- probably in his late
20s or early 30s, for some reason I specifically

00:03:47.049 --> 00:03:51.420
remember his figure shading my eyes and blocking
the now setting sun.

00:03:51.420 --> 00:03:54.439
“Are you part of the lo-fi group?”

00:03:54.439 --> 00:03:59.239
I told him yes, and let him know both my YouTube
username and my real name.

00:03:59.239 --> 00:04:03.569
He told me he was “shadowhand”, which
I instantly recognized as the one who had

00:04:03.569 --> 00:04:06.099
the idea for the meetup in the first place.

00:04:06.099 --> 00:04:10.739
I did notice that he didn’t mention his
real name, which was only a slightly weird

00:04:10.739 --> 00:04:13.489
because I had given him my first name.

00:04:13.489 --> 00:04:17.200
But understanding the somewhat awkward nature
of meeting people from online, I didn’t

00:04:17.200 --> 00:04:21.880
press on the issue, since I didn’t want
to ask anything that might have made him uncomfortable.

00:04:21.880 --> 00:04:26.640
I had also expected someone around the same
age as me, so seeing that he was significantly

00:04:26.640 --> 00:04:28.729
older was also just a bit off-putting.

00:04:28.729 --> 00:04:32.740
He told me that the rest of the group was
already hanging out down the street at one

00:04:32.740 --> 00:04:36.199
of girls’ houses, and that he’d give me
a lift over there.

00:04:36.199 --> 00:04:40.111
His car was parked on the side of the 7/11,
and after locking my bike up to a fence, I

00:04:40.111 --> 00:04:41.960
followed him over towards it.

00:04:41.960 --> 00:04:47.169
I’m fully aware of the dangers of getting
into a stranger’s car, so let me just clarify

00:04:47.169 --> 00:04:49.069
what was going through my head at the moment.

00:04:49.069 --> 00:04:52.450
The first thing that came out of his mouth
when he approached me was about the lo-fi

00:04:52.450 --> 00:04:53.450
group.

00:04:53.450 --> 00:04:56.540
So it’s not like I was just getting picked
up by some rando.

00:04:56.540 --> 00:04:58.639
There were also several of us meeting up.

00:04:58.639 --> 00:05:02.419
So unless this guy made a bunch of YouTube
accounts just to trick me into getting in

00:05:02.419 --> 00:05:03.419
his car…

00:05:03.419 --> 00:05:05.930
I felt like there wasn’t much of a threat.

00:05:05.930 --> 00:05:09.009
He opened the back door of his SUV.

00:05:09.009 --> 00:05:10.669
*ping*

00:05:10.669 --> 00:05:13.780
I received a message from one of the group
members.

00:05:13.780 --> 00:05:15.199
It was from him.

00:05:15.199 --> 00:05:16.660
From ShadowHand1133.

00:05:16.660 --> 00:05:21.690
It said he was in front of the 7/11 and he
was asking if anyone was here.

00:05:21.690 --> 00:05:24.310
I froze in front of the open car door.

00:05:24.310 --> 00:05:28.050
I looked up at the guy, then back down at
my phone.

00:05:28.050 --> 00:05:30.780
“Did you send this?”

00:05:30.780 --> 00:05:36.250
He said, yes, and tried to usher me into the
car, but then for the first time that afternoon,

00:05:36.250 --> 00:05:38.680
something did NOT feel right.

00:05:38.680 --> 00:05:42.460
I turned back and looked at the front of the
store, where I had been waiting before.

00:05:42.460 --> 00:05:47.260
There was a kid standing there, about my age,
looking at a phone.

00:05:47.260 --> 00:05:52.280
What happened next, is still talked about
to this day.

00:05:52.280 --> 00:05:57.190
The kid turned around, and by some stroke
of luck spotted me and waved.

00:05:57.190 --> 00:06:01.379
I turned and waved back, but before I could
tell the man who had offered me a ride that

00:06:01.379 --> 00:06:06.069
there was someone back by the door of the
convenience store, I heard the car door SLAM

00:06:06.069 --> 00:06:07.360
shut behind me.

00:06:07.360 --> 00:06:12.060
The guy literally ran to the driver’s side,
and before I even knew what had happened,

00:06:12.060 --> 00:06:17.129
he was in the car, turning the ignition and
flooring it out of the parking lot, before

00:06:17.129 --> 00:06:24.569
booking it down the road like something out
of a bank robbery scene.

00:06:24.569 --> 00:06:28.349
If you haven’t figured it out yet, I’ll
break it down for you.

00:06:28.349 --> 00:06:32.960
The kid in front of the 7/11 was the real
ShadowHand1133.

00:06:32.960 --> 00:06:37.180
The man in the car was just pretending to
be him since it was a recognizable name from

00:06:37.180 --> 00:06:38.180
the chat.

00:06:38.180 --> 00:06:42.319
We would later figure out that the man with
the car wasn’t anyone from the group who

00:06:42.319 --> 00:06:47.110
had agreed to meet up -- but because we had
planned our get together on a public live

00:06:47.110 --> 00:06:48.699
stream, anyone could see it.

00:06:48.699 --> 00:06:51.240
That was our big mistake.

00:06:51.240 --> 00:06:55.629
Even though all of us were trustworthy, some
random creep noticed our conversation and

00:06:55.629 --> 00:06:57.639
decided to take advantage of it.

00:06:57.639 --> 00:07:02.840
Police would later review the 7/11 security
footage to see the man pull up several minutes

00:07:02.840 --> 00:07:07.680
before I arrived, hiding his SUV along the
side of the building, which was not covered

00:07:07.680 --> 00:07:08.680
by any camera.

00:07:08.680 --> 00:07:09.680
He must have waited there and scoped things
out through his dark tinted windows, then

00:07:09.680 --> 00:07:15.169
upon realizing I was the only one who had
showed up, decided to make his move.

00:07:15.169 --> 00:07:19.819
His license plate was never visible on camera
due to the angle at which he drove in.

00:07:19.819 --> 00:07:23.849
While we do know he was one of the people
tuned into the livestream that day, the police

00:07:23.849 --> 00:07:29.189
had no way of getting an actual list of IP
addresses or accounts who accessed it, soooo….

00:07:29.189 --> 00:07:33.310
to this day, he has never been caught.

00:07:33.310 --> 00:07:37.860
I guess there is one good thing that came
out of all of this though, outside of me really

00:07:37.860 --> 00:07:39.439
putting my guard up.

00:07:39.439 --> 00:07:43.980
The real ShadowHand and I because very good
friends, and it’s always an interesting

00:07:43.980 --> 00:07:47.240
story when people ask how we know each other.

00:07:47.240 --> 00:07:52.139
And no… that isn’t his real username,
I changed it for this story because you can

00:07:52.139 --> 00:07:54.159
never be too careful.

00:07:54.159 --> 00:07:58.669
He and I have spent many hours talking about
what might have happened to me if he had gotten

00:07:58.669 --> 00:08:01.939
there a second later, and I had gotten into
that car.

00:08:01.939 --> 00:08:06.800
It sends shivers down my spine thinking about
what that guy was planning to do or where

00:08:06.800 --> 00:08:10.669
he was planning to take me in that dark-windowed
SUV of his…

00:08:10.669 --> 00:08:16.139
I mean, what kind of kidnapper goes after
random people in a YouTube stream anyway?

00:08:16.139 --> 00:08:21.050
He had no way of knowing who I was, or even
that I would show up to the meet up.

00:08:21.050 --> 00:08:23.479
Let alone the fact that I was there by myself.

00:08:23.479 --> 00:08:25.199
That’s the other thing.

00:08:25.199 --> 00:08:29.280
We later found out that the other kids we
were supposed to meet up with just didn’t

00:08:29.280 --> 00:08:33.050
show up, and decided not to let the group
know they’d no longer be coming.

00:08:33.050 --> 00:08:38.440
I can’t say I blame them for bailing, considering
what almost happened, but it would have been

00:08:38.440 --> 00:08:40.880
nice if they’d given a heads up.

00:08:40.880 --> 00:08:45.810
As far as the lo-fi streams go, yeah, I still
listen to them and partake in the chat too.

00:08:45.810 --> 00:08:50.130
It’s not like I’d be in any kind of danger
just because some freak knows my first name

00:08:50.130 --> 00:08:51.690
and my face.

00:08:51.690 --> 00:08:55.440
But there is something that still bothers
me through this entire experience.

00:08:55.440 --> 00:09:01.010
Every time I write a message in the chat of
that stream… before I press enter, I think

00:09:01.010 --> 00:09:06.000
about the possibility, that that guy with
the SUV is watching, and reading every message

00:09:06.000 --> 00:09:08.750
that I put out...

00:09:08.750 --> 00:09:09.750
--

00:09:09.750 --> 00:09:14.150
*lo-fi song with sound effects*

00:09:14.150 --> 00:09:18.700
I was planning on having my girlfriend over
later that evening, so I threw on some music

00:09:18.700 --> 00:09:20.640
and got to cleaning the place.

00:09:20.640 --> 00:09:24.940
I went upstairs to get started on my room,
since I figured we’d be spending the most

00:09:24.940 --> 00:09:26.530
time there.

00:09:26.530 --> 00:09:31.520
As I was making my bed, I heard what sounded
like someone rummaging around downstairs.

00:09:31.520 --> 00:09:35.180
I do leave the door unlocked when she’s
coming over, but she wasn’t supposed to

00:09:35.180 --> 00:09:39.900
come by for another hour and a half, and early
is not part of her vocabulary.

00:09:39.900 --> 00:09:45.221
It took me a few moments to realize that the
song I was listening to sampling sound bites.

00:09:45.221 --> 00:09:48.660
What I thought I heard was all a part of the
music.

00:09:48.660 --> 00:09:52.890
I finished making my bed and started folding
some of the piles of clothes that covered

00:09:52.890 --> 00:09:54.960
the majority of my bedroom floor.

00:09:54.960 --> 00:09:58.810
*lo-fi music with sound effects*

00:09:58.810 --> 00:10:02.160
No, no that sound had to be coming from downstairs.

00:10:02.160 --> 00:10:06.960
I paused the music and listened closely.

00:10:06.960 --> 00:10:10.070
*roomtone*

00:10:10.070 --> 00:10:14.900
OK, maybe I was right the first time.

00:10:14.900 --> 00:10:16.810
Maybe it was just part of the music.

00:10:16.810 --> 00:10:21.340
I unpaused and sure, enough, the sound that
I thought I had heard was looping in the song.

00:10:21.340 --> 00:10:25.360
I got back to work folding my clothes.

00:10:25.360 --> 00:10:28.830
*lo-fi* *thud*

00:10:28.830 --> 00:10:33.070
OK, that was definitely not part of the song.

00:10:33.070 --> 00:10:44.160
I paused the music yet again, and just as
it paused, I heard a door close down below.

00:10:44.160 --> 00:10:47.960
I called out my girlfriend’s name, to try
to put an end to whatever prank she was pulling

00:10:47.960 --> 00:10:53.950
down there.

00:10:53.950 --> 00:10:58.660
My heart stopped when I saw the scene at the
bottom of the stairs.

00:10:58.660 --> 00:11:04.960
Every single closet, cupboard and drawer was
open, and the contents of each were thrown

00:11:04.960 --> 00:11:06.460
on the ground.

00:11:06.460 --> 00:11:08.260
My place had been ransacked!

00:11:08.260 --> 00:11:13.320
The strange part was, nothing had been taken,
as far as I could tell.

00:11:13.320 --> 00:11:18.270
Whoever was in my house, was looking for one
thing in particular, and I had no idea what

00:11:18.270 --> 00:11:19.760
it was.

00:11:19.760 --> 00:11:24.080
I did a brief search of the ground floor of
my house, but didn’t manage to turn anybody

00:11:24.080 --> 00:11:28.120
up, so I took a seat on the stairs and dialed
9-1-1.

00:11:28.120 --> 00:11:34.130
That’s when I heard noise coming from upstairs
behind me.

00:11:34.130 --> 00:11:38.240
“Who’s there?”

00:11:38.240 --> 00:11:42.700
Whoever had broken into my house had inadvertently
started playing my music again.

00:11:42.700 --> 00:11:44.250
Or maybe it was on purpose.

00:11:44.250 --> 00:11:46.430
I honestly had no idea at this point.

00:11:46.430 --> 00:11:50.000
“Hello? 9-1-1, what’s your emergency.”

00:11:50.000 --> 00:11:52.750
I had nearly forgotten that I was on the phone.

00:11:52.750 --> 00:11:55.320
“I… uhm… there’s someone in my house.”

00:11:55.320 --> 00:11:57.220
“Are you in a safe place where you can talk?”

00:11:57.220 --> 00:11:58.220
...

00:11:58.220 --> 00:12:02.300
I explained the situation, and they recommended
I get to a safe place such as a neighbor’s

00:12:02.300 --> 00:12:03.730
house while they sent someone out.

00:12:03.730 --> 00:12:07.680
I might have been inclined to stay and protect
my belongings, however, the intruder made

00:12:07.680 --> 00:12:12.260
it quite clear he didn’t really care about
valuables, so for the better of my safety

00:12:12.260 --> 00:12:13.860
I took their advice.

00:12:13.860 --> 00:12:17.500
The intruder was never found, and nothing
was taken from my house as far as I could

00:12:17.500 --> 00:12:18.520
tell.

00:12:18.520 --> 00:12:22.750
I don’t leave the door open for my girlfriend
anymore, I made sure to copy her a key after

00:12:22.750 --> 00:12:23.750
that night.

00:12:23.750 --> 00:12:27.180
It’s also made me a bit paranoid whenever
I listen to music.

00:12:27.180 --> 00:12:32.820
I’m constantly pausing if I hear anything
that doesn’t sound instrumental…

00:12:32.820 --> 00:12:34.630
*pause music*

00:12:34.630 --> 00:12:37.620
And if I even think I heard something…

00:12:37.620 --> 00:12:41.720
I’m sure to check all around the house...

00:12:41.720 --> 00:12:42.720
--

00:12:42.720 --> 00:12:49.800
I take a night class on Wednesday evenings
at my university.

00:12:49.800 --> 00:12:54.320
Usually I take an Ubar home, but I was running
a bit low on money and I decided to walk.

00:12:54.320 --> 00:12:56.570
I typically listen to music when I walk.

00:12:56.570 --> 00:12:58.880
Hoodie up and earbuds in.

00:12:58.880 --> 00:13:01.760
When you have long hair like I do, you gotta
keep it dry.

00:13:01.760 --> 00:13:06.640
There was a super light rainpour that night,
not even enough to use an umbrella, just enough

00:13:06.640 --> 00:13:09.460
to where it felt like a nice cool mist with
my hood up.

00:13:09.460 --> 00:13:15.070
So I was just casually walking home, looking
at the ground, not really paying much attention

00:13:15.070 --> 00:13:16.230
to my surroundings.

00:13:16.230 --> 00:13:20.480
I play this little game in my head where I
try to step on each sidewalk tile the same

00:13:20.480 --> 00:13:21.600
amount of times.

00:13:21.600 --> 00:13:25.500
So if I do it, I have like a perfectly paced
walk or something.

00:13:25.500 --> 00:13:28.280
If you don’t get it, I probably can’t
explain it.

00:13:28.280 --> 00:13:33.140
Anyway, I was looking down, and all the sudden,
I nearly step in this huge open manhole in

00:13:33.140 --> 00:13:34.140
the ground.

00:13:34.140 --> 00:13:37.770
I jump back and my heart’s beating out of
my chest, because I nearly just fell down

00:13:37.770 --> 00:13:40.870
and broke my freaking neck at the bottom of
the sewers.

00:13:40.870 --> 00:13:43.260
Who left this sewage cap open to begin with?

00:13:43.260 --> 00:13:45.260
Naturally, I had to look down it.

00:13:45.260 --> 00:13:47.950
It’s not every day you get to see an open
manhole.

00:13:47.950 --> 00:13:51.910
I turned on my phone’s flashlight and peered
down inside.

00:13:51.910 --> 00:13:57.950
What I didn’t expect to see was a pair of
eyes staring back up at me.

00:13:57.950 --> 00:14:02.570
These eyes squinted as if they hadn’t seen
light in days, but that wasn’t the most

00:14:02.570 --> 00:14:03.570
disturbing part.

00:14:03.570 --> 00:14:08.250
This guy’s head was shaved, except for a
maybe a three inch diameter where the hair

00:14:08.250 --> 00:14:10.440
was grown out about 12 inches or so.

00:14:10.440 --> 00:14:14.960
So the result, was he was bald except for
this one messy tube of hair coming out of

00:14:14.960 --> 00:14:16.440
the side of his head.

00:14:16.440 --> 00:14:19.690
He wore a dirty beige jacket, and matching
jeans.

00:14:19.690 --> 00:14:22.250
He also had huge dark bags underneath his
eyes.

00:14:22.250 --> 00:14:27.690
And he immediately cowered away from the light
and hid in one of the pipes down below.

00:14:27.690 --> 00:14:31.330
Not expecting to see someone down there, my
heart skipped a beat and I pulled away from

00:14:31.330 --> 00:14:32.890
the rim of the manhole.

00:14:32.890 --> 00:14:34.290
Who was that?

00:14:34.290 --> 00:14:37.170
No… what was that?

00:14:37.170 --> 00:14:38.230
Maybe I was just overreacting.

00:14:38.230 --> 00:14:41.500
So there’s a homeless guy who takes shelter
in the sewers.

00:14:41.500 --> 00:14:44.530
He probably came up because of all the rain
we’ve been getting, and got a little spooked

00:14:44.530 --> 00:14:45.830
when I saw him.

00:14:45.830 --> 00:14:47.020
As for his haircut?

00:14:47.020 --> 00:14:49.000
Hard to explain that one.

00:14:49.000 --> 00:14:50.340
But he’s living in the sewers.

00:14:50.340 --> 00:14:52.340
He probably had some issues to begin with.

00:14:52.340 --> 00:14:54.330
That’s just the sad truth of the matter.

00:14:54.330 --> 00:14:55.330
I got home.

00:14:55.330 --> 00:14:57.600
Took my shoes off under the awning.

00:14:57.600 --> 00:14:58.600
Tossed my hoodie in the dryer.

00:14:58.600 --> 00:15:01.870
It had gotten more damp than I thought over
the course of the long walk home.

00:15:01.870 --> 00:15:04.740
I went on the computer for a bit before going
to bed.

00:15:04.740 --> 00:15:06.520
That’s when I passed out.

00:15:06.520 --> 00:15:08.470
*text message tone*

00:15:08.470 --> 00:15:11.450
Until I realized my ringtone was still on.

00:15:11.450 --> 00:15:12.450
I went to turn it off.

00:15:12.450 --> 00:15:16.850
I had no interest in replying the message,
until I just happened to notice what it said

00:15:16.850 --> 00:15:17.870
in the preview panel.

00:15:17.870 --> 00:15:21.730
It was from my friend, who lived in the dorms
across the way from me.

00:15:21.730 --> 00:15:24.510
It said, “who’s that by your window?”

00:15:24.510 --> 00:15:25.510
What?

00:15:25.510 --> 00:15:26.590
What was he talking about?

00:15:26.590 --> 00:15:28.440
I reached over for the lightswitch.

00:15:28.440 --> 00:15:29.440
*flips switch*

00:15:29.440 --> 00:15:33.870
There was nothing at my window from what I
could tell.

00:15:33.870 --> 00:15:39.990
At least… that’s what I thought at first…
and I do wish that was the case.

00:15:39.990 --> 00:15:42.670
My window is one of those with a really strong
glare.

00:15:42.670 --> 00:15:47.410
During the day, you can see out from the inside,
but if you try looking in from the outside,

00:15:47.410 --> 00:15:49.450
it’s almost like looking in a mirror.

00:15:49.450 --> 00:15:53.660
But during the night, it’s reversed, to
where it’s hard to see out from the inside,

00:15:53.660 --> 00:15:58.520
but outsiders can see me provided that the
light is on and the blinds are up, which they

00:15:58.520 --> 00:15:59.520
were.

00:15:59.520 --> 00:16:03.640
Although looking out was kind of like looking
through a mirror, there was an unmistakable

00:16:03.640 --> 00:16:05.870
outline of someone standing on the other side.

00:16:05.870 --> 00:16:10.080
There’s only one way to get a better look
out at night, to get your face close to the

00:16:10.080 --> 00:16:12.520
glass and create a shade with your hands.

00:16:12.520 --> 00:16:14.630
And that’s exactly what I did.

00:16:14.630 --> 00:16:17.830
I wish I hadn’t.

00:16:17.830 --> 00:16:22.490
Because for the second time that night, I
saw that terrifying, wild pair of eyes staring

00:16:22.490 --> 00:16:23.490
back at me.

00:16:23.490 --> 00:16:28.150
I only looked out of the window for a slight
moment, before jumping back out of my skin

00:16:28.150 --> 00:16:31.760
and screaming as I reached for my phone to
dial campus security.

00:16:31.760 --> 00:16:38.180
But what I saw in that moment, literally makes
me sick to think about, but I’ll try to

00:16:38.180 --> 00:16:40.970
recount it for the purposes of this story.

00:16:40.970 --> 00:16:46.250
The man at the window, the sewer dwelling
man from before, didn’t have a weird haircut.

00:16:46.250 --> 00:16:48.030
He was actually entirely bald.

00:16:48.030 --> 00:16:53.440
But he had several different colors of hair,
superglued to his head in that one spot.

00:16:53.440 --> 00:16:58.690
Like… like it was his collection or something,
because I also spotted an object in his right

00:16:58.690 --> 00:17:01.600
hand: a rusty pair of scissors.

00:17:01.600 --> 00:17:06.669
I must have screamed the poor security guy’s
ear off, before promptly hanging up, and in

00:17:06.669 --> 00:17:09.959
an act of desperation, pushing my furniture
up to barricade the door.

00:17:09.959 --> 00:17:10.959
*clank.

00:17:10.959 --> 00:17:11.959
Clank.

00:17:11.959 --> 00:17:12.959
clank.*

00:17:12.959 --> 00:17:14.449
But it wasn’t the door I had to be worried,
about, because he started stabbing the scissors

00:17:14.449 --> 00:17:20.019
into the window.

00:17:20.019 --> 00:17:21.659
His taps got harder and harder.

00:17:21.659 --> 00:17:24.809
It didn’t seem like the window would give
much longer before breaking.

00:17:24.809 --> 00:17:29.299
I frantically searched my room for something
to fight back with, but I didn't have much.

00:17:29.299 --> 00:17:32.659
The tapping stopped.

00:17:32.659 --> 00:17:38.559
A bright light flooded the area, and relief
washed over as the campus security pulled

00:17:38.559 --> 00:17:39.559
up.

00:17:39.559 --> 00:17:41.640
I couldn’t hear or see very much through
the glare of the thick window, but from what

00:17:41.640 --> 00:17:45.600
I could tell, the security guard asked the
guy a couple questions, which he promptly

00:17:45.600 --> 00:17:48.870
ignored, and continued to just stare through
my window.

00:17:48.870 --> 00:17:53.289
The guard asked him to leave, and he did comply,
but what still chills me is that he never

00:17:53.289 --> 00:17:58.600
took his eyes off of me the entire time he
was being escorted away, until he was completely

00:17:58.600 --> 00:18:00.029
out of sight.

00:18:00.029 --> 00:18:02.100
The guard caught back up with me later.

00:18:02.100 --> 00:18:04.789
I told him the whole story about the manhole.

00:18:04.789 --> 00:18:08.110
He said I should be careful when walking home
with headphones at night.

00:18:08.110 --> 00:18:12.669
There have been a few cases of people being
followed home by predators, and not noticing

00:18:12.669 --> 00:18:15.200
because they were wearing headphones.

00:18:15.200 --> 00:18:19.799
Usually it’s just some drunk weirdos going
after girls, but as we saw tonight, there

00:18:19.799 --> 00:18:23.150
are just some weird people out there… and
you can never be too careful.

00:18:23.150 --> 00:18:24.970
I asked him what happened with the sewer dweller
guy, and he said that, he basically just kicked

00:18:24.970 --> 00:18:25.970
him off campus and told him he better never
see him here again.

00:18:25.970 --> 00:18:27.840
Other than that, there wasn’t much he could
do, since the guy was on a public walkway

00:18:27.840 --> 00:18:30.000
and didn’t really break any law.

00:18:30.000 --> 00:18:32.799
I always make sure to get a ride home after
night classes now.

00:18:32.799 --> 00:18:41.279
I haven’t seen the guy since then, and I
hope I never do.

00:18:41.279 --> 00:18:42.279
--

00:18:42.279 --> 00:18:50.720
Ahh yes.

00:18:50.720 --> 00:18:55.350
There's nothing quite like the smooth relaxing
sounds of lo-fi when it comes to getting some

00:18:55.350 --> 00:18:57.200
studying done.

00:18:57.200 --> 00:18:58.870
The jazzy chords.

00:18:58.870 --> 00:18:59.899
The bassy undertones.

00:18:59.899 --> 00:19:02.350
The nostalgic samples.

00:19:02.350 --> 00:19:05.230
Something about it is just so...

00:19:05.230 --> 00:19:07.120
Enticing.

00:19:07.120 --> 00:19:09.570
I don't even normally listen to hip-hop.

00:19:09.570 --> 00:19:14.670
When I'm jamming out, I like my music to be
fast loud.

00:19:14.670 --> 00:19:20.470
But when I'm trying to be productive, lyrics
and catchy riffs just distract me.

00:19:20.470 --> 00:19:26.149
But with lo-fi, I can just melt away a whole
pile of work without even realizing it.

00:19:26.149 --> 00:19:33.150
It's just something about the vibes; the atmosphere
created by the combination of this music with

00:19:33.150 --> 00:19:38.789
the scenes of adorable characters doing their
thing on a rainy day or cloudy night.

00:19:38.789 --> 00:19:44.190
Even the people in the chat of each livestream
seem to be easy going and friendly, but I

00:19:44.190 --> 00:19:47.100
try not to get distracted by that too much.

00:19:47.100 --> 00:19:51.010
So today I'm studying for my neurological
science exam.

00:19:51.010 --> 00:19:55.480
We're studying the effects of pavlovian conditioning
and neurophysiology.

00:19:55.480 --> 00:19:58.360
It's easily my favorite course.

00:19:58.360 --> 00:20:02.539
We sometimes even do experiments to see if
we can train small rodents using the concepts

00:20:02.539 --> 00:20:04.230
we studied.

00:20:04.230 --> 00:20:09.129
Sometimes I'd like it if my kid brother, Tevin,
could be trained with such ease, but I seriously

00:20:09.129 --> 00:20:14.470
doubt something like that would ever be possible
on any intelligent being, however low on the

00:20:14.470 --> 00:20:17.830
spectrum of said intelligence he may fall.

00:20:17.830 --> 00:20:19.230
Anddd, what do you know?

00:20:19.230 --> 00:20:20.760
Look who's right on cue.

00:20:20.760 --> 00:20:21.940
Tevin: "Hey bro!

00:20:21.940 --> 00:20:22.940
Whatcha do--"

00:20:22.940 --> 00:20:23.940
Narrator: "--STUDYING..."

00:20:23.940 --> 00:20:24.940
Tevin: "Oh ok.

00:20:24.940 --> 00:20:25.940
So you're bus--"

00:20:25.940 --> 00:20:27.470
Narrator: "YES, I'm busy."

00:20:27.470 --> 00:20:29.049
Tevin: "Oh, that's ok.

00:20:29.049 --> 00:20:33.280
I just wanted to see if you wanted to Robo
Pizza later.

00:20:33.280 --> 00:20:34.280
They're having a--"

00:20:34.280 --> 00:20:38.539
Narrator: "I have an exam on Monday and I'm
already tired."

00:20:38.539 --> 00:20:44.341
Tevin: "Well of course you're tired being
cooped up in here listening to mopey music

00:20:44.341 --> 00:20:45.341
all day.

00:20:45.341 --> 00:20:47.789
Narrator: "It's not mopey music--"

00:20:47.789 --> 00:20:54.490
But before I could even finish objecting,
he, in true rodent fashion, scampered into

00:20:54.490 --> 00:20:58.570
my room and pounced on my laptop, without
permission nor regret.

00:20:58.570 --> 00:20:59.919
*Future funk playlist*

00:20:59.919 --> 00:21:01.909
Narrator: "Ok, you know what Tev?

00:21:01.909 --> 00:21:06.110
I'll take your to your dang pizza place if
you get out now and leave me alone for the

00:21:06.110 --> 00:21:08.419
next hour!"

00:21:08.419 --> 00:21:12.900
In the time it took him to say 'deal' he had
scattered out of my room and SLAMMED the door

00:21:12.900 --> 00:21:14.159
behind him.

00:21:14.159 --> 00:21:17.850
Narrator: "AND TRY NOT TO TOUCH ANYTHING ON
YOUR WAY... out..."

00:21:17.850 --> 00:21:21.480
Well, I'd bought an hour of time to myself.

00:21:21.480 --> 00:21:26.460
And to be totally fair, I actually didn't
mind the Future Funk playlist he had clicked

00:21:26.460 --> 00:21:27.460
on.

00:21:27.460 --> 00:21:28.850
It actually DID wake me up a bit.

00:21:28.850 --> 00:21:33.799
By the end of the night I was feeling OK about
my chances on the test.

00:21:33.799 --> 00:21:36.809
But I still had other homework to finish up.

00:21:36.809 --> 00:21:39.840
So the following night, I found a good lo-fi
stream and..

00:21:39.840 --> 00:21:40.840
*Music*

00:21:40.840 --> 00:21:42.549
Time to get in the zone and knock this thing
out.

00:21:42.549 --> 00:21:43.549
*Music and sfx*

00:21:43.549 --> 00:21:45.929
Now this next part...

00:21:45.929 --> 00:21:48.499
I don't fully know how to describe.

00:21:48.499 --> 00:21:52.039
I was so in the zone doing this mindless work...

00:21:52.039 --> 00:21:54.450
It was almost like I was asleep...

00:21:54.450 --> 00:22:00.620
And without me really realizing it, the music
was getting more and disturbing...

00:22:00.620 --> 00:22:01.620
Off-key...

00:22:01.620 --> 00:22:03.890
And just downright unsettling...

00:22:03.890 --> 00:22:04.890
(Music)

00:22:04.890 --> 00:22:06.870
But it happened so gradually...

00:22:06.870 --> 00:22:10.480
I almost didn't notice it until it was eating
at my anxiety.

00:22:10.480 --> 00:22:18.350
What once relaxed me was now putting me on
a very uncomfortable edge, and for some reason...

00:22:18.350 --> 00:22:19.350
I...

00:22:19.350 --> 00:22:21.999
I didn't have the sense of mind to stop it.

00:22:21.999 --> 00:22:26.210
It was like I was trapped in an unbreakable
loop of tedious work.

00:22:26.210 --> 00:22:32.140
My body wanted to snap out of it but my mind
couldn't come up with the commands to go through

00:22:32.140 --> 00:22:33.140
with it.

00:22:33.140 --> 00:22:39.460
Then, for some unknown reason, I looked at
my laptop screen where the chillhop stream

00:22:39.460 --> 00:22:46.460
was playing, and what I saw affected me so
badly, I felt like I could not even breathe.

00:22:46.460 --> 00:22:52.380
In place of the Kawaii anime girl going her
homework, was some kind of demon.

00:22:52.380 --> 00:23:00.620
A demon whose eyes pierced my soul so badly
I could not look away to end the suffering.

00:23:00.620 --> 00:23:07.019
It curled it's smile in the most unimaginable
way, it almost made me sick.

00:23:07.019 --> 00:23:12.730
It was like it was looking at me specifically,
and it was enjoying putting me under this

00:23:12.730 --> 00:23:13.730
trance.

00:23:13.730 --> 00:23:14.730
*Music cuts*

00:23:14.730 --> 00:23:17.179
I don't remember what happened exactly after
that...

00:23:17.179 --> 00:23:21.410
The next thing I knew, I was standing in my
brother's door-way, not able to remember how

00:23:21.410 --> 00:23:23.809
or why I was there.

00:23:23.809 --> 00:23:27.350
Tevin was staring back at me with a confused
expression.

00:23:27.350 --> 00:23:28.710
Tevin: "Bro?

00:23:28.710 --> 00:23:29.710
Bro!

00:23:29.710 --> 00:23:32.090
What are you doing?"

00:23:32.090 --> 00:23:33.440
Narrator: "I...

00:23:33.440 --> 00:23:34.440
Uh...

00:23:34.440 --> 00:23:35.860
How long have I been standing here?"

00:23:35.860 --> 00:23:37.090
Tevin: "I don't know.

00:23:37.090 --> 00:23:40.760
I was just playing the switch and I randomly
noticed you spacing out at my door.

00:23:40.760 --> 00:23:43.889
I've been trying to wake you up for like two
whole minutes!"

00:23:43.889 --> 00:23:46.230
I cringed at my own unawareness.

00:23:46.230 --> 00:23:48.230
Narrator: "Uhh sorry...

00:23:48.230 --> 00:23:49.730
I just forgot why I came in here."

00:23:49.730 --> 00:23:51.869
Tevin: "Ok...

00:23:51.869 --> 00:23:54.470
Are you on drugs?"

00:23:54.470 --> 00:23:56.830
Narrator: "No!

00:23:56.830 --> 00:23:58.010
No...

00:23:58.010 --> 00:24:02.279
Just really tired I guess."

00:24:02.279 --> 00:24:06.940
Not knowing what else to say, and feeling
embarrassed for myself, I headed back for

00:24:06.940 --> 00:24:08.750
my room.

00:24:08.750 --> 00:24:10.390
Maybe I was right.

00:24:10.390 --> 00:24:12.570
Maybe I did just need some sleep.

00:24:12.570 --> 00:24:18.549
The next day at school I seemed to be totally
recovered.

00:24:18.549 --> 00:24:21.289
I KILLED the science test.

00:24:21.289 --> 00:24:25.840
It felt like I knew every single answer.

00:24:25.840 --> 00:24:28.600
It was overall a really good day.

00:24:28.600 --> 00:24:33.330
The teacher had assigned a project, so after
school it seemed like it was right back to

00:24:33.330 --> 00:24:34.559
work.

00:24:34.559 --> 00:24:38.840
Tevin blabbered something about him wanting
me to take him somewhere as I walked in the

00:24:38.840 --> 00:24:42.429
door but I told him I had a lot of work to.

00:24:42.429 --> 00:24:46.190
For starters, I didn't even have a topic for
my project.

00:24:46.190 --> 00:24:48.179
I needed ideas.

00:24:48.179 --> 00:24:53.860
I went to go turn on some music, when I suddenly
remembered about yesterday.

00:24:53.860 --> 00:25:00.090
The lo-fi, the demon, the randomly finding
myself in my brother's room...

00:25:00.090 --> 00:25:04.460
I typed 🔎 Lo-fi into YouTube to see what
I could turn up and found the same stream

00:25:04.460 --> 00:25:05.789
from yesterday.

00:25:05.789 --> 00:25:08.169
What appeared on the screen before me seemed...

00:25:08.169 --> 00:25:09.200
Normal...

00:25:09.200 --> 00:25:13.210
I looked to the chat to see if there was anything
suspicious.

00:25:13.210 --> 00:25:15.619
I don't know what I thought I'd find.

00:25:15.619 --> 00:25:19.669
There were just some kids having a casual
conversation.

00:25:19.669 --> 00:25:22.460
I then realized how silly it all was.

00:25:22.460 --> 00:25:26.730
I probably just fell asleep doing my homework
and sleepwalked into by brother's room.

00:25:26.730 --> 00:25:31.740
One of our uncles was a known sleepwalker
when he was younger, so it didn't seem so

00:25:31.740 --> 00:25:32.740
crazy.

00:25:32.740 --> 00:25:38.419
Before I could breathe that sigh of relief
though, something sounded kind of off about

00:25:38.419 --> 00:25:39.619
the music.

00:25:39.619 --> 00:25:46.110
I looked back at my screen, where the demon
from before now had it's eyes locked onto

00:25:46.110 --> 00:25:47.110
mine.

00:25:47.110 --> 00:25:49.409
It's cold stare petrified me.

00:25:49.409 --> 00:25:51.390
It reached out towards me.

00:25:51.390 --> 00:25:57.830
It felt like it was literally reaching out
of the screen, though I don't believe it actually

00:25:57.830 --> 00:26:00.230
was possible.

00:26:00.230 --> 00:26:02.999
For whatever reason, I didn't move.

00:26:02.999 --> 00:26:04.210
I didn't scream.

00:26:04.210 --> 00:26:08.100
I didn't click away to another video.

00:26:08.100 --> 00:26:12.419
I felt like it would get me, and I would never
be back!

00:26:12.419 --> 00:26:13.419
...

00:26:13.419 --> 00:26:15.909
That's all I remember...

00:26:15.909 --> 00:26:21.620
The next thing I can recollect was being in
a dark room, not knowing where I was and wondering

00:26:21.620 --> 00:26:23.630
where it had taken me.

00:26:23.630 --> 00:26:30.460
My eyes started to adjust, and what I saw
before me was a face; a face of horror.

00:26:30.460 --> 00:26:36.970
It was my brother, lying in his bed terrified,
looking like he was about to scream bloody

00:26:36.970 --> 00:26:38.110
murder.

00:26:38.110 --> 00:26:41.360
Why was I standing over his bed?

00:26:41.360 --> 00:26:42.970
How did I end up here?

00:26:42.970 --> 00:26:45.519
Tevin: "W-what are you doing?"

00:26:45.519 --> 00:26:46.539
Narrator: "I...

00:26:46.539 --> 00:26:48.160
I don't know.

00:26:48.160 --> 00:26:51.740
I think I've been sleepwalking."

00:26:51.740 --> 00:26:56.610
What he told me next chilled me to the core.

00:26:56.610 --> 00:26:57.610
Tevin: "But...

00:26:57.610 --> 00:26:58.610
Your eyes were open.

00:26:58.610 --> 00:27:00.880
You had the scariest look on your face."

00:27:00.880 --> 00:27:01.880
Narrator: "I..."

00:27:01.880 --> 00:27:07.150
Tevin: "I thought you were gonna hurt me!"

00:27:07.150 --> 00:27:10.429
I was shocked that he would say such a thing.

00:27:10.429 --> 00:27:12.009
I sat down on his bed.

00:27:12.009 --> 00:27:13.429
Narrator: "Tev...

00:27:13.429 --> 00:27:14.429
I...

00:27:14.429 --> 00:27:17.549
You know I would never hurt you..."

00:27:17.549 --> 00:27:18.929
Tevin: "Promise?"

00:27:18.929 --> 00:27:20.999
Narrator: "Of course!

00:27:20.999 --> 00:27:23.320
I would never even think about that...

00:27:23.320 --> 00:27:27.890
I honestly don't remember anything until I
woke up right here."

00:27:27.890 --> 00:27:29.460
Tevin: "OK..

00:27:29.460 --> 00:27:30.460
"

00:27:30.460 --> 00:27:33.880
He didn't sound terribly convinced, but I
told him I'd go back to bed, and asked that

00:27:33.880 --> 00:27:36.450
he let me know if he saw me sleepwalking again.

00:27:36.450 --> 00:27:37.809
*Door close*

00:27:37.809 --> 00:27:38.820
It was late.

00:27:38.820 --> 00:27:44.480
I knew it would probably be an all nighter,
as I still had a ton of homework to get done.

00:27:44.480 --> 00:27:49.639
I also knew I'd probably have to get it done
without the assistance of any lo-fi YouTube

00:27:49.639 --> 00:27:52.350
streams, just to play it safe.

00:27:52.350 --> 00:27:58.169
But when I went back into my room and looked
over all the work I had left, I realized...

00:27:58.169 --> 00:28:00.909
EVERY SINGLE ASSIGNMENT WAS DONE.

00:28:00.909 --> 00:28:03.019
My science project was done too.

00:28:03.019 --> 00:28:08.119
For the first time in my academic career,
I was ahead.

00:28:08.119 --> 00:28:10.620
The next day at school was crazy.

00:28:10.620 --> 00:28:12.570
I got my test back.

00:28:12.570 --> 00:28:14.950
A+. 102%.

00:28:14.950 --> 00:28:20.179
I'd nailed every question and the extra credit.

00:28:20.179 --> 00:28:24.190
In every class, I knew every question the
teacher asked.

00:28:24.190 --> 00:28:33.510
Sometimes I even knew what they were going
to ask before they even said anything.

00:28:33.510 --> 00:28:37.820
Any chance that I'd be studying to any other
sound but the sound of the lo-fi stream that

00:28:37.820 --> 00:28:40.659
night was now out the window.

00:28:40.659 --> 00:28:43.249
When I got home I locked my door.

00:28:43.249 --> 00:28:46.399
Hopefully that would keep me from sleepwalking
into anyone's room.

00:28:46.399 --> 00:28:52.159
Yes, of course I was afraid that I could see
the demon again, but at this point it didn't

00:28:52.159 --> 00:28:53.159
matter.

00:28:53.159 --> 00:28:54.529
It was worth it.

00:28:54.529 --> 00:28:57.980
The stream was waiting for me in my recommended.

00:28:57.980 --> 00:29:03.470
I clicked on it, opened up a book, and started
reading.

00:29:03.470 --> 00:29:05.159
Several minutes went by.

00:29:05.159 --> 00:29:06.980
Nothing happened.

00:29:06.980 --> 00:29:09.999
Possibilities started floating through my
head.

00:29:09.999 --> 00:29:12.970
Maybe it doesn’t work if you're expecting
it.

00:29:12.970 --> 00:29:14.549
Maybe it was a time thing.

00:29:14.549 --> 00:29:18.320
It was earlier than I had started the previous
nights.

00:29:18.320 --> 00:29:22.429
I cranked up the volume until it was as loud
as it would go.

00:29:22.429 --> 00:29:24.020
No effect.

00:29:24.020 --> 00:29:31.129
I figured my best bet was to just try studying
as normal and if it happens it--...

00:29:31.129 --> 00:29:34.590
I heard that familiar sound.

00:29:34.590 --> 00:29:37.119
Things were getting weird with the audio.

00:29:37.119 --> 00:29:41.470
I looked up the screen, expecting to see the
demon staring back at me.

00:29:41.470 --> 00:29:45.419
What I saw instead was the image of an empty
room.

00:29:45.419 --> 00:29:50.429
It was the same room that the anime girl was
usually studying in, but it was just empty.

00:29:50.429 --> 00:29:53.070
But as I turned back to my work...

00:29:53.070 --> 00:29:55.389
I noticed something in the corner of my eye.

00:29:55.389 --> 00:30:01.049
Someone was standing in MY room now, which
I quickly realized was impossible because

00:30:01.049 --> 00:30:02.720
my door was locked.

00:30:02.720 --> 00:30:06.559
The figure stepped forward, and what I saw…

00:30:06.559 --> 00:30:11.739
… what I saw was a life sized version of
the demon from my computer screen, grinning

00:30:11.739 --> 00:30:12.739
at me.

00:30:12.739 --> 00:30:16.029
I fell back out of my chair and slammed on
the ground.

00:30:16.029 --> 00:30:17.820
I'd never been so scared.

00:30:17.820 --> 00:30:23.640
I tried to scramble away but somehow it was
standing over me, smiling that devilish smile.

00:30:23.640 --> 00:30:24.640
It's mouth opened.

00:30:24.640 --> 00:30:26.110
I can’t even properly describe it.

00:30:26.110 --> 00:30:29.019
The mouth opening was probably wider than
a football.

00:30:29.019 --> 00:30:32.590
All I could do was flail at it as it began
to smother me.

00:30:32.590 --> 00:30:36.190
I could hear it's growl take over the sound
of the stream.

00:30:36.190 --> 00:30:39.840
Darkness enveloped me as I could feel the
demon hitting me, in the chest, the arms,

00:30:39.840 --> 00:30:40.840
the face.

00:30:40.840 --> 00:30:43.110
The growl turned into a screech.

00:30:43.110 --> 00:30:44.999
Tevin: "Help!!

00:30:44.999 --> 00:30:45.999
MOM!?

00:30:45.999 --> 00:30:46.999
DAD!?"

00:30:46.999 --> 00:30:50.450
What I saw before me horrified and disgusted
me.

00:30:50.450 --> 00:30:55.940
It was Tevin, on his bed again, but this time
a pair of hands were clenched tight around

00:30:55.940 --> 00:30:56.940
his throat.

00:30:56.940 --> 00:31:02.550
It didn't take me long to realize the horror
of the situation: that they were my hands!!

00:31:02.550 --> 00:31:10.749
And with the lo-fi stream playing audibly
from the other room, I had no control over

00:31:10.749 --> 00:31:11.749
myself.

00:31:11.749 --> 00:31:15.909
I had my brother pinned down to his bed and
I was forcing the air out of him.

00:31:15.909 --> 00:31:19.249
A flash of light filled the room as the door
slammed open.

00:31:19.249 --> 00:31:23.600
My father quickly assessed the situation,
and I was thrown off violently.

00:31:23.600 --> 00:31:29.019
I'd never seen him act so aggressively in
my entire life, and it felt horrible seeing

00:31:29.019 --> 00:31:32.720
him treat me so violently.

00:31:32.720 --> 00:31:35.799
That was a rough night.

00:31:35.799 --> 00:31:39.450
Actually, it was the beginning of a rough
couple of months.

00:31:39.450 --> 00:31:42.259
Luckily, my brother was ok.

00:31:42.259 --> 00:31:43.509
The police came.

00:31:43.509 --> 00:31:46.289
Of course, nobody believed my story.

00:31:46.289 --> 00:31:51.659
I ended up being sent away for a while, but
with no incidents and no sign of mental illness,

00:31:51.659 --> 00:31:55.249
thankfully my stay in the institution didn't
last long.

00:31:55.249 --> 00:31:58.259
The next year I was back in school as normal.

00:31:58.259 --> 00:32:02.820
I had disappeared near the end of the year,
so not too many people even noticed I was

00:32:02.820 --> 00:32:06.419
gone.

00:32:06.419 --> 00:32:11.940
One day in the fall, my curiosity and lack
of closure got the better of me and I muted

00:32:11.940 --> 00:32:16.850
my computer and tried to find stream that
had supposedly set me off.

00:32:16.850 --> 00:32:19.809
I had no intention of listening to it.

00:32:19.809 --> 00:32:22.190
I wanted to report it.

00:32:22.190 --> 00:32:27.160
After a search ended up giving me nothing,
I decided to look back at my browser history.

00:32:27.160 --> 00:32:29.210
There it was.

00:32:29.210 --> 00:32:30.929
I gulped.

00:32:30.929 --> 00:32:36.299
Was it really a good idea to click on it after
several months with no incident?

00:32:36.299 --> 00:32:39.570
I had to know.

00:32:39.570 --> 00:32:40.809
*Click*

00:32:40.809 --> 00:32:42.049
404.

00:32:42.049 --> 00:32:45.239
The page you are trying to access does not
exist.

00:32:45.239 --> 00:32:46.789
I was confused.

00:32:46.789 --> 00:32:48.720
There was an important distinction.

00:32:48.720 --> 00:32:52.970
It didn't say that the stream had been deleted
or the channel had been taken down.

00:32:52.970 --> 00:32:57.279
According to what it said, nothing ever existed
in the first place.

00:32:57.279 --> 00:33:00.480
I decided it wasn't worth wasting any more
of my life on.

00:33:00.480 --> 00:33:04.269
I closed the laptop.

00:33:04.269 --> 00:33:07.740
-2 YEARS LATER-

00:33:07.740 --> 00:33:12.640
That was my last experience with lo-fi for
the next two years.

00:33:12.640 --> 00:33:15.390
I made the effort to avoid it whenever I could.

00:33:15.390 --> 00:33:17.639
I was at my first college party.

00:33:17.639 --> 00:33:21.980
I didn't usually go to parties, but my friend
had convinced me that this one would be pretty

00:33:21.980 --> 00:33:23.879
laid back.

00:33:23.879 --> 00:33:28.700
I shouldn't have been surprised to hear the
sounds of lo-fi chillhop pumping through the

00:33:28.700 --> 00:33:29.700
speakers.

00:33:29.700 --> 00:33:30.980
I took a deep breath.

00:33:30.980 --> 00:33:32.270
Ok.

00:33:32.270 --> 00:33:34.100
I can handle this.

00:33:34.100 --> 00:33:36.309
It's just music at a party.

00:33:36.309 --> 00:33:39.470
If I need to dip outside I can.

00:33:39.470 --> 00:33:44.659
I composed myself and walked into the party
with my friend.

00:33:44.659 --> 00:33:53.409
*Lo-fi goes out of tune*

